Writing tests against the stubs would just assert \"raises `NotImplementedError`,\" which is worthless — instead, here are **spec-driven skeletons for the functions that already have real logic**, and a **TDD skeleton pattern** for the stubs so they exist and start failing-for-the-right-reason the moment Phase 2/3 lands.\n\n### 1.1 `pipeline/schema.py::rule_specificity` — untested, implemented\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_schema.py\nimport pytest\nfrom pipeline.schema import SurvivorshipRule, rule_specificity\n\ndef make_rule(field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"escalate\", **kw):\n    return SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=field, entity_type=entity_type,\n                             strategy=strategy, description=\"d\", **kw)\n\ndef test_wildcard_both_is_least_specific():\n    assert rule_specificity(make_rule(\"*\", \"*\")) == 0\n\ndef test_exact_field_wildcard_entity():\n    assert rule_specificity(make_rule(\"territory\", \"*\")) == 2\n\ndef test_wildcard_field_exact_entity():\n    assert rule_specificity(make_rule(\"*\", \"account\")) == 1\n\ndef test_exact_both_is_most_specific():\n    assert rule_specificity(make_rule(\"territory\", \"account\")) == 3\n\ndef test_prefer_source_requires_preferred_source_id():\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        make_rule(strategy=\"prefer_source\")  # missing preferred_source_id\n\ndef test_prefer_source_with_id_is_valid():\n    rule = make_rule(strategy=\"prefer_source\", preferred_source_id=\"src-a\")\n    assert rule.preferred_source_id == \"src-a\"\n```\n\n**Gap not covered by the spec but worth adding once `select_rule` exists**: two rules with identical specificity — AGENTS.md says \"ties keep author order, first match wins,\" but nothing enforces that ordering is stable across a `list.sort`. Test it explicitly once `select_rule` is implemented (see 1.3).\n\n### 1.2 `pipeline/detect.py::severity_for_orphan` — untested, implemented\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_detect.py\nfrom